WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.755
An agent gets a task: record end lines in graph/extract.py.

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:10.432
Before it edits, it asks one question. What breaks if I change this?

00:00:11.832 --> 00:00:19.569
Reading its way to an answer is costly. extract.py alone is 8,739 lines.

00:00:19.969 --> 00:00:24.892
So it makes one call to Cairn's MCP server: cairn_context.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:30.232
Cairn has already built five layers from this repo, on this machine.

00:00:30.532 --> 00:00:35.632
Map: a tree-sitter code graph. It finds who calls the code being changed.

00:00:36.032 --> 00:00:41.132
Specs: the requirement and the task that own this file.

00:00:41.532 --> 00:00:46.852
Timeline: git history. Two past fixes here, one for UTF-8 on Windows.

00:00:47.252 --> 00:00:52.352
Memory: the decisions and conventions the team recorded.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:58.252
Sessions: an earlier agent found that locations store one line, never a range.

00:00:58.952 --> 00:01:04.052
It all comes back as one pack: ranked, cited and cut to a token budget.

00:01:04.852 --> 00:01:11.963
1,192 tokens, inside a 1,200-token budget. No files copied in.

00:01:12.313 --> 00:01:16.689
Every line names its source, so the agent knows what to verify.

00:01:17.289 --> 00:01:21.389
Now it edits with the blast radius in view.

00:01:22.189 --> 00:01:27.433
cairn_impact confirms it: medium risk, three dependents, two past fixes.

00:01:27.833 --> 00:01:32.832
It writes the range, keeps text I/O in UTF-8, and checks the dependents.

00:01:33.432 --> 00:01:37.932
What it learned goes back with cairn_remember, as one sentence.

00:01:38.282 --> 00:01:42.482
The next session starts with it in the brief. Nothing is learned twice.

00:01:42.832 --> 00:01:46.932
And cairn_session_search finds what any earlier session did.

00:01:47.532 --> 00:01:52.857
None of this needs a model: ASTs, git, spec files and session logs.

00:01:53.207 --> 00:01:58.810
A model only enriches, on Haiku, Sonnet or Opus tiers. It never gates an answer.

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:03.510
Cairn. Institutional memory for coding agents.

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:06.810
One command, in any git repository.
